cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the paper that describes and validates the method."
type: software
title: "blrfit: broad AGN emission lines against the narrow-line systemic velocity"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ektrnddn/blrfit"
authors:
  - family-names: Dadiani
    given-names: Ekaterine
    affiliation: "Carnegie Mellon University"
    email: edadiani@andrew.cmu.edu
keywords:
  - active galactic nuclei
  - broad emission lines
  - spectroscopy
  - supermassive black hole binaries
  - DESI
  - SDSS
abstract: >-
  Fits the broad Halpha, Hbeta and Mg II emission lines of an active galactic nucleus against
  the systemic velocity defined by the narrow lines of the same spectrum, measures the
  displacement and shape of the broad profile, classifies it, flags the conditions under which
  the measurement should not be trusted, and measures velocity changes between epochs by
  chi-square cross-correlation. Works on DESI coadds, SDSS spec files or any wavelength, flux
  and error table.
